[h1] Images

[h2] Basic usage

[p-]
Load an image from podnet or a web URL.
The alt= text is shown if the image fails to load.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/image.gfx]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/image.gfx alt=my image]
[img url=https://example.com/img.png]
[-code]

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx]

[h2] align

[p] Default is center. Options: left, center, right.

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx align=left]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx align=right]
[-code]

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx align=left]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx align=right]

[p-]
When an image is scaled down to fit the content area,
align is ignored and the image is always centered.
[-p]

[h2] resize

[p-]
Default is true. The image scales down to fit if wider
than the content area. Set resize=false to draw at
native pixel size and clip at the edges instead.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx resize=false]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx resize=false align=left]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/img.gfx resize=false align=right]
[-code]

[p-]
With resize=false the align property controls clipping:
center (default) - clipped equally on both sides.
left             - left edge anchored, clipped on right.
right            - right edge anchored, clipped on left.
[-p]

[h2] viewport and cut

[p-]
Show a rectangular region of a larger image.
viewport=X_Y is the top-left corner on the source.
cut=W_H is the width and height of the region.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/sheet.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16]
[-code]

[p] Full image vs a single cropped region (scale=3 to see detail):

[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=8]

[p align=center] full image
[p align=center] viewport=57_7 cut=22_22

[img url=podnet://48932/404.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/404.gfx viewport=57_7 cut=22_22 scale=3 align=center]

[-grid]

[h2] scale

[p-]
scale= multiplies the display size. Useful for showing
small sprites at a readable size. Floats like scale=1.5
are supported. If the result exceeds the content width
it still scales down to fit.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/sheet.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16 scale=2]
[-code]

[p] Same 16x16 sprite at scale=1, 2, and 4:

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto gap=4]

[p align=center] scale=1
[p align=center] scale=2
[p align=center] scale=4

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16 scale=1 align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16 scale=2 align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16 scale=4 align=center]

[-grid]

[link file=how-to/animation.podweb] sprite animation
[link file=how-to.podweb] back to how-to
